        "original_id": "33570fc3-7f1a-5c1e-bd56-5cf7ec9623d7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Singles, songs\n- Systems: Canadian Hot 100\n- Organizations: Billboard\n- Places: Canada\n\nFacts:\n- The Canadian Hot 100 is a singles record chart in Canada that Billboard magazine publishes weekly.\n- In music, a single, record single, or music single is a release type that typically contains fewer tracks than an LP, album, or EP.\n- A single is usually released separately from an album, although it often also appears on an album.\n- The single \"Is Anybody Out There?\" debuted at number 67 on the Canadian Hot 100 and later peaked at number 14.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
